  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off on June 15th and Sarah Tan as the lead. The project has received significant budget approvals, including $500,000 for Phase One, a total executive board approval of $2M covering all phases, and specific allocations for compliance ($55,000), training ($15,000), and team expansion (Mike Chen and Lisa Ray joined). Key activities include a call for AI and data visualization ideas by July 20th, a breakthrough in predictive analytics in Phase Two, and ongoing exploration of a partnership with TechInnovate. Feedback on the prototype is being sought by the end of November, with a detailed progress report scheduled for the staff meeting on November 20th."
